{"obs_mqv8uffn_87f7be0572bc":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_updated","id":"obs_mqv8uffn_87f7be0572bc","raw":{"additions":null,"deletions":null,"files":null,"parentID":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","title":"Fix cold_start + attention + memory_guard (@languages/python-pro subagent)"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:38.913Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8uffp_ebbd6d4f5497":{"observation":{"hookType":"prompt_submit","id":"obs_mqv8uffp_ebbd6d4f5497","raw":{"agent":"languages/python-pro","files":[],"model":{"modelID":"big-pickle","providerID":"opencode"},"parts_summary":["text"],"prompt":"Fix 3 bugs. Read the files first, then apply edits.\n\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py — full scan with hours=999999 (Medium)**\n- Line 48: `list_recent(hours=999999)` loads all 5000 agentmemory episodes on every cold-start check. Fix: Use `search_memory` to check for identity type entries efficiently:\n```python\nexisting = search_memory(\"episodes\", \"identity\", n_results=1, filter_metadata={\"type\": \"identity\"})\nif existing:\n    logger.info(\"Identity already seeded (%d entries found), skipping\", len(existing))\n    return\n```\nYou need to add `from agentmemory import search_memory` to imports. But first check if `search_memory` is already used in the file.\n\nActually, look at the current code first. The function is `cold_start_seeder.seed_if_needed()`. The fix should:\n1. Replace the `list_recent(999999)` call with a targeted `search_memory` call\n2. If results exist, log and return early\n3. The rest of the function stays the same\n\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/attention_filter.py — create_task from sync context (Medium)**\n- Lines 65-70: `asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())` is called from `evaluate()`, a synchronous method called from a watchdog thread. `asyncio.create_task()` requires a running event loop. Fix:\n  - Replace `asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())` with:\n```python\ntask = asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())\ntask.add_done_callback(lambda t: t.exception() and logger.error(\"consolidation failed: %s\", t.exception()))\n```\n  - At minimum, keep the existing try/except but store the task reference and add error callback.\n\nRead the current code to see exactly what's there.\n\n**Bug 3: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/memory_guard.py — validate_memory_write never called (Medium)**\nThis isn't a code fix — it's a wiring issue. Check:\n1. Read `memory_guard.py` to see the `validate_memory_write` API\n2. Read `nexi_gateway.py` to find `store_episode()` calls\n3. If those calls don't have validation, add it.\n\nThe fix should add `validate_memory_write` calls before each `store_episode()` call in nexi_gateway.py:\n```python\nfrom xnch.security.memory_guard import validate_memory_write\n# Before store_episode():\nvalidation = validate_memory_write(content, actor_role, trust_level)\n# If validation fails, return 403 or log warning\n```\n\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed).","variant":null},"sessionId":"ses_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:38.915Z","userPrompt":"Fix 3 bugs. Read the files first, then apply edits.\n\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py — full scan with hours=999999 (Medium)**\n- Line 48: `list_recent(hours=999999)` loads all 5000 agentmemory episodes on every cold-start check. Fix: Use `search_memory` to check for identity type entries efficiently:\n```python\nexisting = search_memory(\"episodes\", \"identity\", n_results=1, filter_metadata={\"type\": \"identity\"})\nif existing:\n    logger.info(\"Identity already seeded (%d entries found), skipping\", len(existing))\n    return\n```\nYou need to add `from agentmemory import search_memory` to imports. But first check if `search_memory` is already used in the file.\n\nActually, look at the current code first. The function is `cold_start_seeder.seed_if_needed()`. The fix should:\n1. Replace the `list_recent(999999)` call with a targeted `search_memory` call\n2. If results exist, log and return early\n3. The rest of the function stays the same\n\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/attention_filter.py — create_task from sync context (Medium)**\n- Lines 65-70: `asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())` is called from `evaluate()`, a synchronous method called from a watchdog thread. `asyncio.create_task()` requires a running event loop. Fix:\n  - Replace `asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())` with:\n```python\ntask = asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())\ntask.add_done_callback(lambda t: t.exception() and logger.error(\"consolidation failed: %s\", t.exception()))\n```\n  - At minimum, keep the existing try/except but store the task reference and add error callback.\n\nRead the current code to see exactly what's there.\n\n**Bug 3: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/memory_guard.py — validate_memory_write never called (Medium)**\nThis isn't a code fix — it's a wiring issue. Check:\n1. Read `memory_guard.py` to see the `validate_memory_write` API\n2. Read `nexi_gateway.py` to find `store_episode()` calls\n3. If those calls don't have validation, add it.\n\nThe fix should add `validate_memory_write` calls before each `store_episode()` call in nexi_gateway.py:\n```python\nfrom xnch.security.memory_guard import validate_memory_write\n# Before store_episode():\nvalidation = validate_memory_write(content, actor_role, trust_level)\n# If validation fails, return 403 or log warning\n```\n\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed)."},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8ufg1_3d544dd70105":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_status","id":"obs_mqv8ufg1_3d544dd70105","raw":{"attempt":null,"message":"","status_type":"busy"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:38.928Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8ufg2_3739483cdf06":{"observation":{"hookType":"assis